{"sectionId":"renal/water-acid","items":[{"id":"renal--water-acid-k001","sectionId":"renal/water-acid","unitId":"renal","subject":"biology","text":"유효 순환량 감소 또는 macula densa NaCl 전달 감소는 renin 분비를 촉진할 수 있다.","kind":"body-derived","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"renal--water-acid-k002","sectionId":"renal/water-acid","unitId":"renal","subject":"biology","text":"renin은 angiotensinogen을 Ang I으로, ACE는 Ang II로 전환한다.","kind":"body-derived","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"renal--water-acid-k003","sectionId":"renal/water-acid","unitId":"renal","subject":"biology","text":"Ang II는 혈관수축, aldosterone 분비, 갈증 및 ADH 반응을 촉진한다.","kind":"body-derived","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"renal--water-acid-k004","sectionId":"renal/water-acid","unitId":"renal","subject":"biology","text":"ADH는 V2–Gs–cAMP–PKA를 통해 집합관의 AQP2 삽입을 증가시키고 basolateral AQP3/4를 통해 물이 빠져나간다.","kind":"body-derived","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"renal--water-acid-k005","sectionId":"renal/water-acid","unitId":"renal","subject":"biology","text":"aldosterone은 mineralocorticoid receptor를 통해 ENaC 및 Na⁺/K⁺ ATPase 등의 발현·활성을 조절한다.","kind":"body-derived","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"renal--water-acid-k006","sectionId":"renal/water-acid","unitId":"renal","subject":"biology","text":"혈액의 대표 완충계는 CO₂/HCO₃⁻이다.","kind":"body-derived","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"renal--water-acid-k007","sectionId":"renal/water-acid","unitId":"renal","subject":"biology","text":"pH≈6.1+log([HCO₃⁻]/(0.03×PaCO₂))로 표현할 수 있다(농도 mmol/L, 압력 mmHg).","kind":"body-derived","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"renal--water-acid-k008","sectionId":"renal/water-acid","unitId":"renal","subject":"biology","text":"호흡은 CO₂, 신장은 bicarbonate 재흡수와 새로운 bicarbonate 생성 및 산 배설을 조절한다.","kind":"body-derived","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"renal--water-acid-k009","sectionId":"renal/water-acid","unitId":"renal","subject":"biology","text":"대사성 산증은 HCO₃⁻ 감소, 호흡성 산증은 PaCO₂ 증가가 일차 변화다.","kind":"body-derived","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"renal--water-acid-k010","sectionId":"renal/water-acid","unitId":"renal","subject":"biology","text":"신장의 NH₄⁺와 적정산 배설은 순산 배설에 기여한다.","kind":"body-derived","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"renal--water-acid-k011","sectionId":"renal/water-acid","unitId":"renal","subject":"biology","text":"보상은 원인과 별개이며 일반적으로 pH를 완전히 정상화하지 않는다.","kind":"body-derived","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"renal--water-acid-k012","sectionId":"renal/water-acid","unitId":"renal","subject":"biology","text":"ADH는 물 재흡수, aldosterone은 Na⁺ 보존·K⁺ 분비에 중요.","kind":"highlight","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"renal--water-acid-k013","sectionId":"renal/water-acid","unitId":"renal","subject":"biology","text":"V1a는 Gq 혈관수축, V2는 Gs 물 재흡수.","kind":"highlight","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"renal--water-acid-k014","sectionId":"renal/water-acid","unitId":"renal","subject":"biology","text":"요붕증은 ADH 부족 또는 신장 반응 저하에 의해 발생할 수 있다.","kind":"highlight","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"renal--water-acid-k015","sectionId":"renal/water-acid","unitId":"renal","subject":"biology","text":"산염기 장애는 pH, PaCO₂, HCO₃⁻의 일차 변화를 함께 본다.","kind":"highlight","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"renal--water-acid-k016","sectionId":"renal/water-acid","unitId":"renal","subject":"biology","text":"소변량은 감소하고 삼투농도는 증가한다.","kind":"review-answer","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]}]}